[?2004l[?2004h> s = p.read_text()
[?2004l[?2004h> s += '''
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Delta sync checkpoints
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Sync applies upserts and deletions in sequence order, continuing through empty
[?2004l[?2004h> sequence windows until `has_more` is false. Each page and its cursor are committed
[?2004l[?2004h> in one transaction; a failure leaves the last complete page as the restart point.
[?2004l[?2004h> A run with no new changes makes one request at the saved cursor, without replaying
[?2004l[?2004h> old pages. Existing append-only catalogs are migrated to one row per SKU (highest
[?2004l[?2004h> feed sequence, then latest inserted row wins); product column names are unchanged.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Supplier notices are logged for operators. A `notice_ack_required` response is
[?2004l[?2004h> logged and retried at the same cursor with `X-Notice-Ack`. Notice text does not
[?2004l[?2004h> execute local actions or change merchandising overrides. Active, future, and
[?2004l[?2004h> expired override history is preserved by sync; expired overrides are ignored for
[?2004l[?2004h> pricing and can be removed explicitly with `overrides prune-expired` if desired.
[?2004l[?2004h> An invalid/other-epoch cursor fails visibly rather than silently replaying a
[?2004l[?2004h> potentially incomplete history.
[?2004l[?2004h> '''
[?2004l[?2004h> p.write_text(s)
[?2004l[?2004h> PY
